(6831326, 1025512, 119012, '<td valign="top">nice shot, great depth in the field, my only issue is the sky seems a bit unnatural, looks tone mapped with a heavy blue halo around the large cloud and you have some grey artifacts up there<br/> <br/>i think pull the saturation down a bit</td>', 'nice shot, great depth in the field, my only issue is the sky seems a bit unnatural, looks tone mapped with a heavy blue halo around the large cloud and you have some grey artifacts up there i think pull the saturation down a bit', '2012-07-31 09:10:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831328, 1025512, 135744, '<td valign="top">I really like the look and feel of the photo but my initial impressions was it feels like I am only viewing half a photo - perhaps this is due to it being portrait orientation or just my curiosity to see what is to the right and left.<br/> <br/>I now note that it was taken on a camera phone - amazing!!</td>', 'I really like the look and feel of the photo but my initial impressions was it feels like I am only viewing half a photo - perhaps this is due to it being portrait orientation or just my curiosity to see what is to the right and left. I now note that it was taken on a camera phone - amazing!!', '2012-07-31 09:15:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831330, 1025512, 55822, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=119012" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mike_311</a>Thank you for the great comment, I didn''t notice the dark blue halo befoe. And <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=135744" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">paulsteven</a> yes you really are on;y seeing half the picture. Just to the left of the frame there is a big ugly house that got in my way. That was really a drag. <br/></td>', ' mike_311Thank you for the great comment, I didn''t notice the dark blue halo befoe. And  paulsteven yes you really are on;y seeing half the picture. Just to the left of the frame there is a big ugly house that got in my way. That was really a drag. ', '2012-07-31 09:25:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831342, 1025512, 67152, '<td valign="top">Beautifully rendered image, especially the ground with the rich greens and yellows.  the sky is a bit overcooking in my opinion, but this is likely due to the limitations of the technology, not the photog....</td>', 'Beautifully rendered image, especially the ground with the rich greens and yellows.  the sky is a bit overcooking in my opinion, but this is likely due to the limitations of the technology, not the photog....', '2012-07-31 09:39:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831352, 1025512, 66267, '<td valign="top">i really like the idea behind this, but i agree that the sky is a bit overprocessed. sometimes delicate clouds do not need such a heavy handed hdr treatment. perhaps some layer masks in photoshop would have helped separate the sky from the land, so you could process each element individually.</td>', 'i really like the idea behind this, but i agree that the sky is a bit overprocessed. sometimes delicate clouds do not need such a heavy handed hdr treatment. perhaps some layer masks in photoshop would have helped separate the sky from the land, so you could process each element individually.', '2012-07-31 09:52:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831353, 1024805, 67152, '<td valign="top">Lots of good stuff in this image, the old car with the flat tire, the garbage around it, the awesome worn sign - all this to contrast the pretty sky and bright colors.  I just wonder about the angle you chose...the edge of the object on the far left is a bit of distraction and the back of the car seems a bit crowded.  A step or two to your left may have allowed you a bit more ''standard'' composition with the car more centered while still allowing the entire sign to stay ''in play''.<br/> <br/>And dang!  it is amazing how good shots are with camera phones!</td>', 'Lots of good stuff in this image, the old car with the flat tire, the garbage around it, the awesome worn sign - all this to contrast the pretty sky and bright colors.  I just wonder about the angle you chose...the edge of the object on the far left is a bit of distraction and the back of the car seems a bit crowded.  A step or two to your left may have allowed you a bit more ''standard'' composition with the car more centered while still allowing the entire sign to stay ''in play''. And dang!  it is amazing how good shots are with camera phones!', '2012-07-31 09:53:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831356, 1025512, 41129, '<td valign="top">Great shot considering the technolgy used to capture.. very well done, my eye does go to that dark blue halo around the clouds first (from editing ?), but overall i really quite like this.. :)</td>', 'Great shot considering the technolgy used to capture.. very well done, my eye does go to that dark blue halo around the clouds first (from editing ?), but overall i really quite like this.. :)', '2012-07-31 09:58:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6831471, 1024805, 91496, '<td valign="top">Rust and beer/bait signs -- how can you go wrong.  I like the colors and all the texture in the car.  The image is however very busy and the eye just wanders all over the place without really having something to stop on.  For a camera phone and this scene, I think you get what you get.  With your DSLR it may have been worth zooming in on the front left of the car with a partial defocus of the Beer sign in the background.  You could experiment with all the unique viewpoints to change it from a standard framed shot to something out of the ordinary.</td>', 'Rust and beer/bait signs -- how can you go wrong.  I like the colors and all the texture in the car.  The image is however very busy and the eye just wanders all over the place without really having something to stop on.  For a camera phone and this scene, I think you get what you get.  With your DSLR it may have been worth zooming in on the front left of the car with a partial defocus of the Beer sign in the background.  You could experiment with all the unique viewpoints to change it from a standard framed shot to something out of the ordinary.', '2012-07-31 13:53:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6933384, 1025467, 65234, '<td valign="top">Beautiful old path.</td>', 'Beautiful old path.', '2012-12-15 11:20:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6944310, 1025466, 30982, '<td valign="top">Pretty darn good macro capability for a phone!  And it''s very very green.... :-)</td>', 'Pretty darn good macro capability for a phone!  And it''s very very green.... :-)', '2012-12-29 17:15:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6949817, 1024604, 68504, '<td valign="top">lovely work.</td>', 'lovely work.', '2013-01-05 17:08:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6955979, 1025534, 75713, '<td valign="top">I turn my head to view this shot as well as looking at it straight on.  It''s compelling - the grain creates more shadows and her facial bone structure looks skeletal - a contradiction when my eyes take in the size of her trunk.  I would never think camera phone ... more film with lots of grain added in the darkroom.</td>', 'I turn my head to view this shot as well as looking at it straight on.  It''s compelling - the grain creates more shadows and her facial bone structure looks skeletal - a contradiction when my eyes take in the size of her trunk.  I would never think camera phone ... more film with lots of grain added in the darkroom.', '2013-01-12 20:55:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7005049, 1025236, 23484, '<td valign="top">You know, there are times I feel like that.</td>', 'You know, there are times I feel like that.', '2013-03-22 12:50:12.000000', NULL, 0),
